==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|cæremonial}} {{qualifier|[[Appendix:Glossary#archaic|archaic]]}}

===Etymology====
From {{inh|en|enm|cerymonial}}, from {{der|enm|la|caerimōniālis}}. 

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-ceremonial.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Of, relating to, or used in a [[ceremony]]; [[ritual]] or [[formal]].
#* Hallam
#*: '''Ceremonial''' observances and outward show.
# {{lb|en|archaic}} Observant of forms; [[ceremonious]].
#: {{rfquotek|John Donne}}
#* John Dryden
#*: He moves in the dull '''ceremonial''' track.

